{
  "description": "A2A skills as tools (PROTOCOL.md §5.4): one tool per skill of the Agent Card, in card order. name: the skill id (else its name) with each run of characters outside [A-Za-z0-9_.-] replaced by _ and trimmed of _; description: the skill's description, else its name, or null when both are empty. A skill is a data skill when its inputModes (else the card's defaultInputModes) name a JSON media type (one containing json); otherwise, with no modes at all included, it is a text skill. A data skill's tool has inputSchema {type: object} and no outputSchema: agent.json supplies the schemas. A text skill's tool takes and returns one text field: inputSchema {type: object, properties: {text: {type: string, description: \"What to ask the agent\", examples: the skill's string examples, when it has any}}, required: [text], additionalProperties: false} and outputSchema {type: object, properties: {text: {type: string, description: \"The agent's answer\"}}, required: [text]}. A skill declares no hints: the publisher settles the class. calls: a text skill is sent its text field as the message's one text part, and answers with structured content {text: its text parts joined by a newline}; a data skill is sent its arguments as one data part, and answers with its first data part that is an object as structured content.",
